  "term": "APP",
  "definition": "APP is the gene and protein known as amyloid-beta precursor protein. It helps with receptor-related cell signaling at the cell surface and can be cut by secretases into several products, including soluble peptides, membrane-bound fragments, amyloid plaque components, regulatory molecules, and neurotoxic fragments.",
